cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GSW Memory, please cite the AAAI 2026 paper below. If you use the continual-learning setting, please also cite Panini (ICML 2026)."
title: "GSW Memory: Generative Semantic Workspaces"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/roychowdhuryresearch/gsw-memory"
abstract: >-
  Generative Semantic Workspaces (GSW) is a structured episodic memory for LLMs
  and LLM agents. An Operator maps incoming text to actors, roles, states and
  space-time anchors, and a Reconciler merges them into a persistent workspace
  that stays temporally, spatially and logically coherent. The workspace serves
  as long-term memory for retrieval-augmented generation and for non-parametric
  continual learning.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - episodic memory
  - long-term memory
  - LLM memory
  - structured memory
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - continual learning
  - Generative Semantic Workspace
  - EpBench
